{
 "schema": "fd-deposit-candidate/1",
 "labels": {
  "what": "the 5D result on its sixteen reporting cells R00-R15: cell definitions, the measured vector f, the revised covariance C_total + C_resp + C_PL5D and its correlation matrix",
  "status": "candidate, not deposited: nothing is uploaded and no DOI is minted until Joseph releases it",
  "order": "every vector and matrix is in the cell order R00, R01, ..., R15 (cells.csv's row order)",
  "units": "f: each cell's integrated cross section, cm^2/nucleon (a cell integral, not a differential density); covariance: (cm^2/nucleon)^2; sigma = sqrt(diag(covariance)), cm^2/nucleon; box edges: p_T and p_parallel in GeV/c, E_avail, q3 and W in GeV",
  "edges": "the upper edge 100 GeV on E_avail, q3 and W is the analysis grid's last edge: the last bin on those axes is a catch bin to 100 GeV; 4.5 GeV/c on p_T and 60 GeV/c on p_parallel are the grid's outer edges too. A cell's integral covers only its box inside the grid; no edge is infinity",
  "covariance": "C_total + C_resp + C_PL5D = C_e + C_model_abs + C_resp + C_PL5D, the revised reported covariance (the with-block data product's C_total_plus_C_resp_plus_C_PL5D). The paper's chi2 for a prediction g on its cells c is d^T (C + V_g)^-1 d with d = f - g, C this covariance on c, and V_g = diag of g's own finite-MC variance, ndf n; its shape-only chi2 adds 100 f f^T (f on c, absolute units) to C + V_g, ndf n - 1; g and V_g are the prediction's, not part of the measurement",
  "gibuu": "GiBUU is compared on the eight cells with p_parallel < 4.5 GeV/c only (gibuu_subset = 1)",
  "unreported": "the sixteen cells cover 28 of the 32 H2 boxes; the four unreported boxes are listed with their bounds and are in no cell",
  "not_citable_for": "coverage; any reading, claim or release text",
  "block": "C_PL,5D: the 5B run-period block (FD-CT-5B-REPORT.md), audited (FD-CT-5B-AUDIT-REPORT.md); added after the data were seen; published with and without. Its sigma rests on three periods: the 68% interval on sigma_true/sigma_hat is [0.73, 2.56]. Noise-dominated cells: R00, R08. Rank 2; undebiased",
  "decision": "added under DECISION-20261030 item 2 after the audit's stop condition did not fire (FD-CT-5B-AUDIT-REPORT.md); the decision followed the data; published with and without",
  "context_dr_pair": "descriptive; not a reason for the addition: the best detector-response pair (GEANT_Pion#1 with C_resp:meson#1) explains 0.853, 0.560 and 0.617 of PA's, PB's and PC's noise-weighted offset patterns at |a| <= 1.51, reproducing PA's to within noise and not PB's or PC's; pairs have no stop role (FD-CT-5B-AUDIT-REPORT.md section 4)",
  "context_5a_5b": "descriptive; not a reason for the addition: 5A's and 5B's mean period offsets agree, PB -2.724% against -2.699% and PC +4.671% against +4.806%, while their patterns about the mean differ beyond the combined noise, with sum (Delta/sigma)^2 of 81.6 and 192.8 over 16 cells (FD-CT-5B-AUDIT-REPORT.md section 6)"
 },
